el improves  as the name suggests they're podcast  based lessons which is great for people  who like to learn using audio materials  and for people who want to learn on the  go  these days i try to focus much more on  audio materials than i used to  so that i can build my listening  comprehension and do my best to imitate  native pronunciation but class 101 and  pod 101 courses  offer more than just audio lessons they  have lots of video lessons as well as  downloadable books and pdf materials  so that you can get visual input and  explanations of all the language  introduced in the lessons  they also have audio recordings of the  individual words and phrases so you can  review them individually  and you can create vocabulary flash  cards that use spaced repetitions to  help you memorize the words more easily  they also offer quizzes to help you  review lessons word lists of the most  commonly used words and other features  for class 101 and pod 101 courses in  general i recommend using the additional  tools such as the downloadable lesson  notes and the spaced repetition  flashcards  to review and solidify what you learn in  each lesson before moving on to the next  one  for danish specifically i really  recommend you focus on the lesson  vocabulary words and their recordings so  that you can hear each individual word  clearly pronounced and  imitate it if you have an awareness of  the features of danish pronunciation  like those mentioned in this video  and then you practice imitating the  pronunciation of the individual words  while observing their spelling  that should be of tremendous help in  taking on danish phonology  i've never learned a language using only  a class 101 or pod 101 course but i'm a  member of several of their courses and i  regularly use them as part of my study  program  lots of content is free including all  new lessons which are free for the first  couple of weeks  and then if you want access to all the  content you can upgrade to a paid  account  i really recommend you check out  innovative language courses  whether for danish or one of 33 other  languages they offer  click the link in the description to get  a free lifetime account  i also want to give a big shout out to  all the lang focus patreon supporters  especially the top tier patrons whose  names are on the screen  check out patreon.com langfocus and  check out the benefits of the various  tiers  and to everyone thank you for watching  and have a nice  [Music]  day  [Music]  you
 

